.TH AGENT-HOOK-NOTIFICATION 1 "2026-11-11" "agentguard" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
agent-hook-notification \- play terminal notifications for agent events
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B agent-hook-notification
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B agent-hook-notification
reads an agent notification hook payload from standard input and plays the
configured terminal notification sound through
.BR "term-notify-sound \-\-owner" ,
naming the agent process so that an agent it launched cannot mark its pane
pending, and passes the kind of attention with
.BR \-\-kind .
It leaves the busy tmux pane mark alone and does not add workflow warnings or
blocks.
.TP
.B waiting
A permission prompt or question: a
.B Notification
whose
.B notification_type
(or
.BR notificationType )
is
.BR permission_prompt ,
.BR elicitation_dialog ,
or Gemini CLI's
.BR ToolPermission ,
and the
.B PermissionRequest
event Codex and the OpenCode adapter deliver to this hook. After the mark is
set, the hook records the session's
.I attention-sticky
flag: the kind and the actor that raised it (the root agent, or the child
routed by
.B agent_id
or a Muse child session). Claude names no actor on permission
notifications, a subagent's included, so its flag accepts any actor.
A glance does not acknowledge a waiting mark; the agent's next tool, the end
of the child that raised it, or the end of the turn or session clears it (see
.BR agent-hook-telemetry (1)).
It always rings and records its flag, even from a turn the hooks did not see
start (its Stop is then fenced, and its next tool or the next prompt clears
the mark).
.TP
.B idle_prompt
Claude Code sends this about a minute after the agent goes idle. It clears a
waiting mark (a prompt dismissed with Esc ends no turn) and rings
.B done
only if it wins the prompt cycle's single bell, which a ringing
.BR agent-hook-stop (1)
already holds, or once for a Stop that found that bell taken (a turn that
started without a prompt), so it is the backstop for a turn whose Stop did
not ring.
.BR agent-hook-telemetry (1)
still repairs the busy mark from it.
.TP
.B auth_success
Nothing.
.TP
.B done
Any other notification, as before.
.PP
An older
.B term-notify-sound
that rejects
.B \-\-kind
(exit status 64) is called again without it, which rings and sets a plain
pending mark, and no flag is recorded.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The notification was emitted or skipped by best-effort terminal handling.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR agent-hook-stop (1),
.BR agent-hook-telemetry (1),
.BR term-notify-sound (1),
.BR term-pane-mark (1)
